h1 Manifest: an overview
h2 What it is
text Manifest is a way for an AI agent to put things on a screen and to see what is there, through one text tree. The agent writes MX, a compact one-node-per-line format; the engine lays it out, paints it, takes the user's input; and the agent reads the screen back as the same text, with the engine's own layout boxes and a short list of diagnostics, instead of a screenshot.
text Three decisions make it work:
text "One vocabulary of roles with defaults. button \"Export CSV\" disabled is nine tokens and the renderer owns the look. Any node may take a position, a size and paint children, so the same tree can draw a funnel, a floor plan or a gauge down to the pixel, and every painted thing still carries a label and a role. Use the highest level that is faithful."
text Perception is the format. observe returns MX, so whatever the agent reads it can patch. Level 1 is the semantic tree; level 2 adds boxes; level 3 adds every shape. A since= query returns only what changed, as a patch.
text One engine. The core, the renderer, the host with lifecycle and input, and the MCP server are one Rust codebase that runs as a native window, headless, or as WebAssembly in the browser, with no browser dependency of its own.
h2 How it works
text agent ──MX──▶ engine ──pixels──▶ screen ▲ │ └──MX+boxes───┘ observe, since=, look, events
text Parse: one line per node, IDs derived from labels, errors that name the line.
text Layout: flexbox and grid through taffy, text shaped from the bundled Inter font, sized nodes as coordinate spaces for positioned children, nested default looks for positioned nodes without paint.
text Paint: tiny-skia, at the screen's pixel density, light and dark palettes.
text "Host: surfaces, revisions, lifecycle (ttl, seen, until, ephemeral, residues), pointer and key input that produce action and input events, tweens for nodes marked anim:."
text Perception: from the engine's own boxes, with !overflow, !overlap, !contrast, !tiny and !offcanvas.
text Transport: MCP over stdio, or the same calls from JavaScript against the wasm build.
h2 What it costs, measured
text All counts with Claude's tokenizer; reader accuracy with fresh Haiku readers that saw only the text. Full tables in .
link bench/results.md results.html
table Col MX "best alternative"
  Six everyday visuals, tokens to create | 788 | 1,762 (A2UI Atom), 4,521 (HTML)
  Sixteen edits | 238 | 622 (HTML find and replace)
  Read back, level 1 | 828 tokens, 30 of 30 questions | 1,544 tokens, 27 of 30 (cropped screenshots)
  Six paint-heavy visuals | 2,685 | 6,104 (HTML + SVG + ARIA), 6,645 (A2UI paint catalog)
  Read back, paint-heavy, level 1 and 3 | 27 and 30 of 30 | 
  A page imported from HTML | 1,158 | 4,569 (the HTML), 1,463 (accessibility snapshot)
  A hundred real pages imported | 736,715 | 6,510,211 (the HTML)
h2 Where it sits
text (Google) covers the write side: declarative components, no code, streaming. Manifest adds perception and lifecycle, and  proposes both as A2UI v1.0 extensions with MX as an inference format; the compiler exists.
text A2UI
link docs/a2ui-extension.md a2ui-extension.html
text MCP Apps and browser agents give models a UI or a page and a screenshot back. Manifest gives the tree back, and the engine is the only thing that paints it.
text HTML paints everything but tells a model nothing about what it painted. The importer (import/) reads a rendered page and writes MX with semantics first and paint where nothing semantic fits.
h2 Limits
text Coordinates are expensive in any text format and models place things badly. The format's answer is defaults and layout owned by the engine; the loop's answer is observe level 2 and the !overlap and !offcanvas diagnostics.
text Level 1 drops unlabelled shapes by design, so arrows that carry meaning need labels or a flow.
text "Buffers hold key:value numbers; each over records is not there yet."
text The importer demotes a chart drawn with divs to paint; reading its values from an aria-label sentence is the next step.
text No 3D, no keyframe animation, no plugin widgets.
text Manifest is Apache-2.0.
link "Source, issues and discussion on GitHub." https://github.com/brunopgalvao/manifest
